---
/**
 * Objection handling, set as a ruled list of native disclosures. Serif
 * questions, hairline rules, plain +/− marker. The composition answer is
 * deliberately mechanism-honest without naming implementation details.
 */
const faqs = [
	{
		q: 'What do you mean by "spacious clarity"?',
		a: "It's the result of the practice: continuous, vivid appreciation of experience. It's not blankness or numbness. Practitioners describe it as more room around experience",
	},
	{
		q: "I've never meditated. Can I start here?",
		a: "Yes. The course assumes no experience, and the first sessions build the foundation: how to sit, what to do with thoughts, how to return. Beginners sometimes have an advantage; there's less to unlearn.",
	},
	{
		q: 'I already meditate. Will this be remedial?',
		a: "No. Different systems aim at different results, and this one aims somewhere specific. Don't buy the platitude that all paths lead to the same goal; empirically, this is not so. Opening Awareness works by release not concentration, and many practitioners arrive from vipassana, TMI, or years of app practice. The first ten days help you recalibrate, you don't start again from scratch.",
	},
	{
		q: 'Is this religious?',
		a: 'No. The practice descends from a Tibetan lineage: Opening Awareness is a contemporary adaptation of a practice called shi-né. The course is designed for experiment not belief. Nothing to join, no vocabulary to adopt.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Is this therapy?',
		a: "No. Meditation and therapy develop different capacities, and this course isn't a treatment for anything. Opening Awareness can sit well alongside therapy, and many practitoners find it steadying. If you're in acute crisis or working through trauma, therapy first is often the right order; the course will still be here.",
	},
	{
		q: 'How much time does it take?',
		a: 'You get to choose, consistency matters more than duration. The aim is a habit that fits your real, ordinary life. Missed days are not failure. The course adapts to you rather than scolds.',
	},
	{
		q: 'How long until I notice anything?',
		a: "Honestly, it varies. With regular practice, many people notice changes in the quality of attention within weeks; understanding the instruction deeply can take a year or more. Day-to-day changes usually show up before the method feels clear. We'd rather undersell this than promise you a schedule.",
	},
	{
		q: 'How are sessions composed?',
		a: "Every word of teaching is Charlie's, recorded and written in advance. The course software chooses which teaching, which sit, which question comes next, based on what happens as you practice.",
	},
	{
		q: 'The course makes itself unnecessary. Then what?',
		a: "You keep the practice; that's the point. The course fades toward a simple timer and a library you can browse when curious. And if you want teachers, peers, and practices beyond Opening Awareness, Evolving Ground is the wider community this grew out of.",
	},
	{
		q: 'What will it cost?',
		a: "$249 as a one-time purchase, not subscription. We don't want to optimize for keeping you around. We want this to work for you in whatever way is best.",
	},
	{
		q: `Doesn't "uninvolved" mean detachment?`,
		a: "It points the opposite direction. You practice remaining uninvolved during a sit so that clarity is available when you're fully involved in life. Nothing is pushed away. Thoughts and feelings come and go. You discover they no longer define experience.",
	},
];
---

<section class="faq-section" id="questions" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
	<div class="sheet">
		<h2 id="faq-heading" class="faq-heading">Questions</h2>

		<div class="faq-list">
			{
				faqs.map((item) => (
					<details class="faq-item">
						<summary>
							<span class="faq-question">{item.q}</span>
							<span class="faq-marker" aria-hidden="true" />
						</summary>
						<p class="faq-answer">{item.a}</p>
					</details>
				))
			}
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.faq-section {
		background: var(--surface);
		padding: clamp(3rem, 4vw + 1rem, 5.5rem) 0 clamp(3.5rem, 5vw + 1rem, 6.5rem);
	}

	.faq-heading {
		font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 1.2rem + 1.8vw, 2.6rem);
		font-weight: 390;
		letter-spacing: -0.016em;
		line-height: 1.1;
		margin: 0 0 clamp(1.25rem, 2vw, 2rem);
	}

	.faq-list {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	.faq-item {
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	.faq-item summary {
		display: flex;
		align-items: baseline;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding: 1.1rem 0;
		cursor: pointer;
		list-style: none;
	}

	.faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
		display: none;
	}

	.faq-question {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: 1.25rem;
		font-weight: 430;
		line-height: 1.35;
		color: var(--ink);
	}

	.faq-marker {
		flex: 0 0 auto;
		position: relative;
		width: 0.85rem;
		height: 0.85rem;
		transform: translateY(0.1em);
	}

	.faq-marker::before,
	.faq-marker::after {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		background: var(--ink-soft);
	}

	.faq-marker::before {
		inset: 50% 0 auto 0;
		height: 1.5px;
		transform: translateY(-50%);
	}

	.faq-marker::after {
		inset: 0 auto 0 50%;
		width: 1.5px;
		transform: translateX(-50%);
		transition: transform 200ms ease;
	}

	.faq-item[open] .faq-marker::after {
		transform: translateX(-50%) scaleY(0);
	}

	.faq-item summary:hover .faq-question {
		color: var(--ink-soft);
	}

	.faq-answer {
		max-width: var(--measure);
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0 0 1.35rem;
		font-size: 1.125rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
		color: var(--ink-soft);
	}
</style>
